WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.076 --> 00:00:20.383
One beautiful October morning, Marilla and Anne sat in the kitchen and cut vegetables.

2
00:00:20.384 --> 00:00:26.675
"Anne," Marilla began, "why don't you ask Diana to come over for afternoon tea?

3
00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:29.755
I am going into town, and she can come then."

4
00:00:29.756 --> 00:00:35.541
"Oh, Marilla!" Anne clasped her hands. "How perfectly lovely!

5
00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:40.711
We will be like grown-ups! Can we use the teapot with the roses?"

6
00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:47.301
"No, but I have some cake and raspberry cordial in the pantry you can have," Marilla replied.

7
00:00:47.302 --> 00:00:51.403
Diana came over, dressed in her second-best dress.

8
00:00:51.404 --> 00:00:57.760
Anne, dressed in her own second-best dress, opened the door with a very serious expression.

9
00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:00.210
Together they went to the front room.

10
00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:03.988
"How is your mother?" Anne asked politely, like an adult.

11
00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:10.308
"She is very well, thank you. And Mr. Cuthbert is in the potato fields?" asked Diana.

12
00:01:10.309 --> 00:01:16.355
"Yes, he is. Our potatoes are very good this year," replied Anne.

13
00:01:16.356 --> 00:01:23.714
Abruptly her tone changed. "Oh Diana!" she burst out. "Let's go and pick some apples!"

14
00:01:23.715 --> 00:01:29.977
The girls instantly stopped acting like proper ladies and ran outside to the apple orchard.

15
00:01:29.978 --> 00:01:33.992
"Marilla said we can pick the rest of the apples," said Anne.

16
00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:40.628
"Marilla is very kind. She also said we can have cake and raspberry cordial for tea.

17
00:01:40.629 --> 00:01:45.264
I love red drinks—they just taste better, don't they?"

18
00:01:45.265 --> 00:01:51.204
Later the girls went inside, and Anne went to the pantry to get the raspberry cordial.

19
00:01:51.205 --> 00:01:56.184
At first she couldn't see it anywhere, but then she spotted it at the back.

20
00:01:56.185 --> 00:01:59.638
Anne put the cordial on the table with a big glass.

21
00:01:59.639 --> 00:02:05.122
"Please help yourself, Diana. I can't drink a thing after eating all those apples."

22
00:02:05.123 --> 00:02:08.883
Diana poured herself some of the drink and sipped it.

23
00:02:08.884 --> 00:02:12.359
"This is a very nice cordial, Anne," she said.

24
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.337
"I didn't know cordial tasted so good."

25
00:02:15.338 --> 00:02:21.718
"I'm glad you like it," Anne replied. "Take as much as you want. I'll get the cake."

26
00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:26.295
When Anne came back, Diana was drinking a second glass of cordial.

27
00:02:26.296 --> 00:02:30.387
Diana started to drink a third glass, and Anne didn't mind.

28
00:02:30.388 --> 00:02:34.415
"It's the nicest cordial I ever drank," said Diana.

29
00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:40.455
"It's much nicer than Mrs. Lynde's cordial. It doesn't taste a bit like hers."

30
00:02:40.456 --> 00:02:45.873
"I'm sure Marilla's cordial is nicer than Mrs. Lynde's," said Anne loyally.

31
00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:52.529
"Marilla is a famous cook. She's trying to teach me, but it's hard work, Diana.

32
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:59.268
Last week," Anne continued, "Marilla told me to put some pudding sauce in the pantry and cover it.

33
00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.846
I took the bowl of sauce into the pantry, but I forgot to cover it.

34
00:03:03.847 --> 00:03:07.192
I remembered the next morning and ran to the pantry.

35
00:03:07.193 --> 00:03:11.252
Diana, a mouse had drowned in the sauce!

36
00:03:11.253 --> 00:03:14.776
I used a spoon to get the mouse and took it outside.

37
00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:18.447
Then I was going to tell Marilla about the mouse.

38
00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:26.112
But I started pretending I was a forest fairy flying through the trees, and I forgot about the mouse and the sauce.

39
00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:29.836
After that Mr. and Mrs. Ross came for lunch.

40
00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:37.919
We ate lunch and everything was fine until I saw Marilla coming in with plum pudding and pudding sauce, warmed up.

41
00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:44.771
I remembered everything and shouted, 'Marilla, don't use the sauce. A mouse drowned in it!'

42
00:03:44.772 --> 00:03:49.751
Mr. and Mrs. Ross looked at me, and I thought I would die!

43
00:03:49.752 --> 00:03:55.600
Why, Diana," Anne said suddenly. "What's the matter?"

44
00:03:55.601 --> 00:04:00.518
Diana stood up and then sat down, putting her hands to her head.

45
00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:07.483
"I'm . . . I'm very sick," she said. "I . . . I must go home."

46
00:04:07.484 --> 00:04:11.975
"No, don't go yet. You must eat some cake first."

47
00:04:11.976 --> 00:04:15.162
"I must go home," Diana repeated.

48
00:04:15.163 --> 00:04:17.925
"Where do you feel bad?" Anne asked.

49
00:04:17.926 --> 00:04:21.426
"I'm very dizzy," said Diana.

50
00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:26.389
Anne was very disappointed, but she took Diana to the Barrys' fence.

51
00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:31.122
The next day Marilla sent Anne to Mrs. Lynde's house on an errand.

52
00:04:31.123 --> 00:04:36.765
In a short space of time, Anne came flying back to Green Gables in tears.

53
00:04:36.766 --> 00:04:39.804
"What's the matter, Anne?" Marilla said.

54
00:04:39.805 --> 00:04:47.387
"Mrs. Lynde saw Diana's mother today. Mrs. Barry said that I sent Diana home drunk.

55
00:04:47.388 --> 00:04:56.032
And she said I was a very wicked girl and she's never, never going to let Diana play with me again!"

56
00:04:56.033 --> 00:05:05.316
"Diana was drunk?" Marilla was stunned. "Anne, are you or Mrs. Barry crazy? What did you give her?"

57
00:05:05.317 --> 00:05:15.045
"Nothing but raspberry cordial," Anne said. "I never thought it made you drunk, not even if you drink three glasses like Diana did."

58
00:05:15.046 --> 00:05:20.631
Marilla marched to the pantry. On the shelf was a bottle of homemade wine.

59
00:05:20.632 --> 00:05:28.525
At that moment Marilla remembered that the cordial was in the cellar and not the pantry as she had told Anne.

60
00:05:28.526 --> 00:05:34.793
Marilla went back into the kitchen. "Anne, you gave Diana wine instead of cordial!

61
00:05:34.794 --> 00:05:37.132
Don't you know the difference between them?"

62
00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:42.788
"I didn't taste the drink," said Anne. "Only Diana drank it.

63
00:05:42.789 --> 00:05:46.526
And then Diana got so sick and went home.

64
00:05:46.527 --> 00:05:54.743
Mrs. Barry said Diana just laughed and laughed, and then slept for hours, and had a headache all day.

65
00:05:54.744 --> 00:05:59.022
Her mother smelled her breath and knew she was drunk."

66
00:05:59.023 --> 00:06:03.910
"Three glasses of cordial would make you sick," Marilla said, troubled.

67
00:06:03.911 --> 00:06:08.754
"But it was an accident, Anne, so don't worry. I'll talk to Mrs. Barry."

68
00:06:08.755 --> 00:06:13.582
At that, Marilla left. When she came back later, she was frowning.

69
00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:17.524
"Was Mrs. Barry still angry?" asked Anne.

70
00:06:17.525 --> 00:06:24.665
"Mrs. Barry?" snapped Marilla. "I told her it was a mistake, but she didn't believe me.

71
00:06:24.666 --> 00:06:33.213
So I told her that if my girl was so greedy, drinking three glasses of anything, I'd be punishing her!"

72
00:06:33.214 --> 00:06:40.873
Marilla went into the kitchen. Anne stepped outside, and she walked determinedly to the Barrys' house and knocked on the door.

73
00:06:40.874 --> 00:06:47.790
When Mrs. Barry saw it was Anne, she frowned. "What do you want?" she demanded.

74
00:06:47.791 --> 00:06:53.471
Anne clasped her hands. "Oh, Mrs. Barry, please forgive me.

75
00:06:53.472 --> 00:06:59.910
I did not mean to . . . to make Diana . . . drunk. How could I?

76
00:06:59.911 --> 00:07:05.406
She is my best friend in the world. I thought it was raspberry cordial.

77
00:07:05.407 --> 00:07:08.555
Please say that you'll let me play with Diana.

78
00:07:08.556 --> 00:07:15.850
If I can't play with her, my life will be covered by a huge dark cloud of sadness."

79
00:07:15.851 --> 00:07:19.843
Anne's dramatic plea had no effect on Mrs. Barry.

80
00:07:19.844 --> 00:07:23.773
She said coldly, "Anne, you should go home.

81
00:07:23.774 --> 00:07:27.377
You are not a good friend for Diana."

82
00:07:27.378 --> 00:07:33.249
"Can't I see Diana and just say one last good-bye?" Anne asked.

83
00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:38.161
"Diana is out with her father," said Mrs. Barry, shutting the door.

84
00:07:38.162 --> 00:07:41.765
Anne walked back to Green Gables with her head down.

85
00:07:41.766 --> 00:07:47.235
"My last hope is gone," she told Marilla, full of despair.

86
00:07:47.236 --> 00:07:52.028
"I talked to Mrs. Barry, and she treated me very badly.

87
00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:55.022
I can do nothing now but pray.

88
00:07:55.023 --> 00:08:02.215
But I don't think that will help because even God can't change Mrs. Barry's mind."

89
00:08:02.216 --> 00:08:08.802
"Anne, don't talk like that," said Marilla, trying not to laugh at Anne's theatrics.

90
00:08:08.803 --> 00:08:16.494
But later Marilla couldn't help feeling pity for Anne when she saw that the child had cried herself to sleep.

91
00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:26.908
"Poor little thing," Marilla whispered, kissing Anne's red cheek.
